          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "pernottare is a learned borrowing from Latin pernoctāre 'to stay all night', built from per and nox, noctis 'night' (Lewis & Short)."
            }
          ]
        },
